From 1787e9cb880d1442aed60f3f1f505e29a088c8dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stel777 <274792865+Stel777@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 20:02:44 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] feat(vaults): re-add the grid view for the vault manager
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Upstream v0.6.0 took the sortable vault list but not the grid, and a 260px
single column is a long scroll once there are dozens of vaults.

Grid widens the panel to min(76vw, 760px) and tiles the vaults with
auto-fill/minmax columns, so the count of columns follows the window instead
of being fixed. Each row gains a border + radius in grid mode only (in list
mode the panel already separates them, so a border would just add noise), and
the active vault is outlined in the accent colour. The choice persists in
localStorage next to the sort key, and both views share the same sort.

Re-anchored rather than copied: the 0.5.2 version expanded to fill the space
beside the sidebar via a [data-neurovault-sidebar] lookup, which does not
exist on this path — the selector now lives in Settings -> Open vault manager.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/components/BrainSelector.tsx | 82 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 78 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/components/BrainSelector.tsx b/src/components/BrainSelector.tsx
index d454bc8..29c2dac 100644
